The [[2026 NFL season|2026 season]] is the [[Kansas City Chiefs]]' 57th in the [[National Football League]] (NFL), their 67th overall, their tenth under the leadership of general manager [[Brett Veach]] and their 14th under [[List of Kansas City Chiefs head coaches|head coach]] [[Andy Reid]]. The Chiefs will seek to improve upon their 6–11 record from [[2025 Kansas City Chiefs season|2025]], make the playoffs after a one-year absence, and reclaim the AFC West title. 

The Chiefs started 5–0 for the second time in three seasons, and became the last undefeated team in the AFC. 

Because [[Pittsburgh Steelers]]' coach [[Mike Tomlin]] resigned and the [[Baltimore Ravens]] fired [[John Harbaugh]], Andy Reid is now the longest-tenured active head coach (with one team, and with multiple consecutively) in the NFL, with his tenure starting in the [[2013 Kansas City Chiefs season|2013 season]] with the Chiefs.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gering |first=Brett |title=Kansas City Chiefs Hire Andy Reid as New Head Coach |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/1466869-kansas-city-chiefs-hire-andy-reid-as-new-head-coach |access-date=2026-10-04 |website=bleacherreport.com |language=en}}</ref>
