The Broncos came from behind to defeat the Chiefs 28–24 at home, seizing the top spot in the AFC West. The Chiefs had held a 24–13 lead heading into the fourth quarter; however, quarterback Bo Nix led an offensive surge, resulting in 15 unanswered points. With less than two minutes remaining, Patrick Mahomes drove the Chiefs deep into opposing territory, but on the game’s final play—a 4th and goal attempt—defensive lineman Malcolm Roach recorded a sack to seal the victory for Denver. With this result, the Broncos improved to 6–2 and took over the top spot in their division.

